  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/tests/winding_align.rs`: the test `the_inside_out_stl_fixture_reads_inside_out_and_refuses` becomes `the_inside_out_stl_fixture_is_turned_outward_at_import_and_lays`.\n- `docs/decisions/1752-inside-out-fixture-test.md`: the decision entry.\n\nNo product code changes.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #1686 (#1672) turns a closed, isolated inward STL/OBJ body outward at import. The import also adds a note. This is the intended behaviour, and the PR has a decision entry and its own pins. The old test still expected the refusal from before #1686. The PR #1686 quick gate did not run `winding_align`, so main became red after the merge.\n\nThe failure is deterministic. The test failed in 5 of 5 local runs on origin/main 4141eb1 with `left: [Outward]`, `right: [InsideOut]`.\n\n## Pinned behaviour\n\nThe new test reads `testdata/models/cube_inside_out.stl` and checks these items:\n\n- The import gives one note. The note says that 1 closed solid was turned outward and that 12 facets were reversed.\n- The imported body reads as `Outward`.\n- `load_model` gives the same mesh as `load_model_graded`.\n- The top face lays (flip) with a half turn, as the outward block does.\n\nNo refusal is loosened. These tests still pin the refusals:\n\n- `an_inside_out_cube_refuses_the_face_lay_by_name`, `an_inside_out_cube_refuses_the_321_by_name` and `bodies_are_judged_one_by_one` pin the refusal of an inside-out body that reaches the world unturned.\n- `nested_stl_cavity_is_refused_before_normalization` and `nested_obj_cavity_is_refused_before_normalization` (`import_outward.rs`) pin the import refusal of a nested inward shell, which the importer cannot turn safely.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate test the_inside_out_stl_fixture --crate camcraft-app --binary winding_align` on origin/main: FAIL (the reproduction).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test winding_align`, 5 runs: 9 passed each time.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (`app:winding_align`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test winding_align -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The other app suites and the batch tier. The post-merge gate runs them after the merge.\n- The GUI. The GUI was not started.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1752\n",
